From: GSL Fix <gsl-fix@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Remove space in GSL_SUPPRESS: add WhitespaceSensitiveMacros and remove clang-format guards

clang-format was inserting spaces in GSL_SUPPRESS arguments, e.g.
GSL_SUPPRESS(r.11) -> GSL_SUPPRESS(r .11), which breaks the
[[gsl::suppress("r.11")]] attribute matching after macro expansion.

Fix by:
1. Adding WhitespaceSensitiveMacros: ['GSL_SUPPRESS'] to .clang-format
2. Removing all // clang-format off/on guards around GSL_SUPPRESS usages

---
 .clang-format                        | 2 ++
 include/gsl/algorithm                | 2 --
 include/gsl/assert                   | 2 --
 include/gsl/narrow                   | 4 ----
 include/gsl/span                     | 26 --------------------------
 include/gsl/util                     | 6 ------
 tests/notnull_tests.cpp              | 16 ----------------
 tests/strict_notnull_tests.cpp       | 8 --------
 8 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 66 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.clang-format b/.clang-format
--- a/.clang-format
+++ b/.clang-format
@@ -33,3 +33,5 @@
 SpaceAfterCStyleCast: true
 CommentPragmas: '^ NO-FORMAT:'
+
+WhitespaceSensitiveMacros: ['GSL_SUPPRESS']
diff --git a/include/gsl/algorithm b/include/gsl/algorithm
--- a/include/gsl/algorithm
+++ b/include/gsl/algorithm
@@ -49,5 +49,3 @@

     Expects(dest.size() >= src.size());
-    // clang-format off
     GSL_SUPPRESS(stl.1) // NO-FORMAT: attribute
-    // clang-format on
     std::copy_n(src.data(), src.size(), dest.data());
diff --git a/include/gsl/assert b/include/gsl/assert
--- a/include/gsl/assert
+++ b/include/gsl/assert
@@ -94,5 +94,3 @@
